# --- Stabilization pass: generated / cache / machine-local (see REPOSITORY_STABILIZATION_MANIFEST.md) ---
# wrangler local cache (regenerated by `wrangler dev`)
cloudflare-worker/.wrangler/
# prior-agent run logs
tools/claude-wired-runs/
# generated harness bundle (source is src/renderer/__devharness__ + root *-harness.html)
harness-dist/
# generated Blanc report (reproducible: tools/blanc-budget.cjs --update)
/blanc-budget.json
# NOTE: blanc-coverage.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is not a generated
# report — nothing reproduces it. It is the hand-maintained triage manifest that
# tools/blanc-drift.cjs reads (deliberately-excluded reasons, dated coverage
# notes), and the drift script throws if it is missing. It was ignored in 54fd5d9
# alongside blanc-budget.json; that made the drift gate unrunnable in CI and on a
# fresh clone. Un-ignored 2026-07-21.
# stray artifact
/.search-result.txt
# machine-local agent / MCP / automation config
/.claude/settings.json
/.mcp.json

# Mooncap full-track ambient bed (yt-dlp from youtube.com/watch?v=g33LSGLwLzo;
# ~118MB opus — regenerate locally, do not commit)
src/renderer/assets/reading-garden/audio/*.opus
src/renderer/assets/reading-garden/audio/*.webm
!src/renderer/assets/reading-garden/audio/.gitkeep

# --- Publication prep: internal doc corpus (ruling R4, docs/audit/RULINGS_2026-08-04.md) ---
#
# DELIBERATELY COMMENTED OUT. This block belongs to the .gitignore of the NEW
# public repo that ruling R2 creates — NOT to this private repo.
#
# It was briefly active on 2026-08-04 and immediately did harm here: `docs/audit/`
# matches *untracked* files, so six audit documents (four authored that day) went
# invisible to `git status` and could never have been committed. R2 keeps this
# private repo WITH FULL HISTORY, so silently dropping the audit trail from it is
# the opposite of what was ruled. Verified before and after with:
#     git check-ignore -q -- docs/audit/FINDINGS_P2C_GRAMMARX_PROBE_F.md
#
# Note also that .gitignore never untracks what is already tracked: the 50 files
# in `git ls-files docs/audit` would have stayed in history regardless. Exclusion
# only works from a repo's first commit, which is exactly the R2 flow.
#
# TO USE: paste the block below into the fresh public repo's .gitignore BEFORE its
# first `git add`. Why exclusion rather than sanitizing (R4): these carry absolute
# machine paths, account addresses, agent dispatch text, and detailed findings
# about defects with no shipped fix. Sanitizing 50+ documents is larger, more
# error-prone, and one miss is a permanent disclosure.
#
#   docs/audit/
#   docs/migration/
#   .coordination/
#   src/.coordination/
#   CLAUDE.md
#   .claude/skills/
#   DISPATCH_*.md
#   HANDOFF_*.md
#   FINDINGS_*.md
#   /grammar-audit.json
#   archive/
#
#
# --- RESOLVED 2026-08-05 (C1-7): the 36 root-level docs are now one line ---
#
# The `archive/` entry added to the block above replaces the whole measurement
# that used to live here. On 2026-08-05, 33 of the 37 tracked root-level `.md`
# files were `git mv`d into `archive/`, leaving only PROJECT.md, TASKS.md,
# AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and (new) FEATURES.md at the root. CLAUDE.md is already
# listed above; the rest are documents a public repo reasonably has.
#
# So the 36-file publication decision this section used to describe is now a
# single pattern, which is the point of the move.
#
#   git ls-files -- '*.md' | grep -v /      # 4 files, was 37
#
# STILL TRUE AND STILL THE OWNER'S CALL: whether PROJECT.md, TASKS.md, AGENTS.md
# and FEATURES.md ship. Nothing here is active.
#
# The four files that carried content the 2026-07-28 scrub or R4 would remove are
# all inside `archive/` now, so they are covered by the one pattern:
#
#   archive/GRAMMARX_REDESIGN_PLAN.md              32 x pre-de-branding module name
#   archive/UI_MIGRATION_DEBT.md                    5 x absolute C:\\Users\\<user> paths
#   archive/REPOSITORY_RECOVERY.md                  4 x absolute C:\\Users\\<user> paths
#   archive/REPOSITORY_STABILIZATION_MANIFEST.md    2 x absolute C:\\Users\\<user> paths
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING THE MOVE ACHIEVED PRIVACY. Moving a file does NOT
# remove it from git history. Every one of these 33 documents remains in this
# repo's history at its old root path, forever, exactly as before. `archive/`
# makes FUTURE publication clean; it scrubs nothing retroactively. A genuinely
# clean public repo means a fresh repo with no imported history — which is what
# R2/R4 already anticipate, and is the only flow in which this block does its job.
#
# `/grammar-audit.json` is listed for two reasons: it is reproducible
# (`node tools/grammar-audit.cjs --compare` rewrites it), and the committed copy
# still carries pre-de-branding source-module identifiers that the 2026-07-28
# scrub removed everywhere else — see F21 in AUDIT_2026-08.md.
